From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:04:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 178/178] DeepSeek V4.1 encoding: current-turn thinking across
 tool results, tool images in prompt order

DeepSeek's encoding fix of 2026-10-16 (both V4.1 Flash checkpoints):
- A user message holding only tool results no longer starts a turn: the
  current turn's reasoning is kept across its tool results and dropped once a
  new user message completes the turn.
- Media is collected after tool results take the order the assistant called
  them. vLLM collects media from the request's messages before encoding, so
  the DS4.1 renderer now applies order_tool_results first: it permutes each
  merged turn's tool messages exactly as merge_tool_messages and
  sort_tool_results_by_call_order arrange their blocks, and the encoder then
  reorders nothing; each image follows its own placeholder.
- Image tokens in text (content, text parts, reasoning) are rejected, for every
  role.

The fixtures follow the new reference (the 1017 encoder; all earlier cases
are unchanged under it) and add its current-turn and tool-image cases.
